``` 

Please note that this solution requires visual studio environment which has debug statements. C# compiler does not recognize debug statements like "Debug.Assert()". Debug.Assert() is for debug purposes to quickly halt the execution and look into the details of the error and the state of the variables/conditions. This is not compiled within the C# library. It is a language feature provided by Windows, .NET, or Mono that's not part of the C# specification.--------------------
Debug.Assert(New_arrListIndexOfX >= 0);
</code>--------------------
